  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-1,$ ${x}_{2}=4,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$ Find $P(x).$",
  "worked_solution": "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-1,$ ${x}_{1}=4,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =1(x-(-1))(x-4)(x-5) \\\\  & =(x+1)(x-4)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)(x-4)(x-5) & =({x}^{2}-3x-4)(x-5) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-5{x}^{2}+15x-4x+20 \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+11x+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+11x+20.$",
